<article class="env-remark" id="06JA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06JA">Remark <span data-tag="06JA">90.16.9</span>.</a> We say that a functor $F: \mathcal{C}_\Lambda \to \textit{Sets}$ is a <em>deformation functor</em> if the associated cofibered set is a deformation category, i.e. if $F(k)$ is a one element set and $F$ satisfies (RS). If $\mathcal{F}$ is a deformation category, then $\overline{\mathcal{F}}$ is a predeformation functor but not necessarily a deformation functor, as Lemma <a href="/tag/06J8" data-tag="06J8">90.16.7</a> shows. </p>
</article>